# HIGH LEVEL SYSTEM DESIGN

```text
Customer Orders
       ↓
Kafka Producer
       ↓
Kafka Topic
       ↓
PySpark Streaming Consumer
       ↓
Bronze Layer (Raw)
       ↓
Silver Layer (Cleaned)
       ↓
Gold Layer (Business KPIs)
       ↓
Snowflake Warehouse
       ↓
Streamlit Dashboard
```

---

# LOW LEVEL DESIGN

```text
Producer:
    generate_orders.py

Kafka:
    order_topic

Consumer:
    spark_streaming_job.py

Transform:
    cleanse + deduplicate + enrich

CDC:
    detect INSERT / UPDATE

SCD Type 2:
    maintain customer history

Warehouse:
    fact_orders
    dim_customers

Orchestration:
    Airflow DAG

Dashboard:
    Streamlit KPIs
```

# Snowflake Data Engineer Stack

| Tool/Skill             | What It Does in Data Engineering Pipeline                      |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| SQL                    | Query, transform, filter, aggregate data                       |
| Python                 | Automation, ETL scripting, API integration, data processing    |
| ETL / ELT              | Moving and transforming data from source to destination        |
| Airflow                | Schedules and orchestrates pipelines (runs jobs automatically) |
| Snowflake              | Cloud Data Warehouse where analytics data is stored            |
| dbt                    | Creates transformation models inside Snowflake using SQL       |
| AWS                    | Cloud platform hosting data infrastructure                     |
| S3                     | Data lake/storage layer for raw files                          |
| CDC                    | Captures only changed records instead of full loads            |
| SCD Type 1 & 2         | Tracks historical changes in dimension tables                  |
| Data Modeling          | Designs tables and relationships for reporting                 |
| Star Schema            | Optimized model for BI reporting                               |
| Snowflake Schema       | Normalized warehouse model                                     |
| JSON                   | Semi-structured data format often received from APIs           |
| Parquet                | Compressed analytics-friendly file format                      |
| Avro                   | Schema-based data exchange format                              |
| Git                    | Version control for code                                       |
| Docker                 | Creates consistent development environments                    |
| GitHub Actions/Jenkins | Automates deployment and testing                               |
| REST APIs              | Source system from which data is extracted                     |
| IAM/Roles              | Controls user permissions and security                         |
| Monitoring & Logging   | Tracks pipeline failures and performance                       |
| Query Optimization     | Improves SQL execution speed                                   |
| Clustering             | Improves Snowflake query performance                           |
| Tableau                | Business dashboards and reports                                |
| Power BI               | Business intelligence visualization                            |
| Streamlit              | Creates data applications and dashboards using Python          |
| Great Expectations     | Validates data quality automatically                           |
| Window Functions       | Advanced SQL analytics operations                              |
| Stored Procedures      | Reusable SQL business logic                                    |

